 "sections": [
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Reading a cash-flow table"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "A cash-flow table shows **money in** and *money out* by month. See [the guide](https://example.com/guide) and the term [[cash flow]]."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "prior",
   "text": "You already know that a budget is a plan for money."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "outcome",
   "text": "By the end you can read a cash-flow table and name the weakest month."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "place",
   "text": "This sits after budgeting and before forecasting."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "story",
   "text": "A baker in Kisumu noticed flour costs rose every March."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "jargon",
   "text": "Cash flow means money moving in and out, not profit."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "book",
   "text": "Small changes compound over years.",
   "citation": "Housel, The Psychology of Money, ch. 4"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "research",
   "text": "Households that track spending save more on average.",
   "citation": "Smith et al., 2019, J. Fin. Behav."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "fact",
   "text": "Mobile money moved over a trillion shillings last year."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "probe",
   "text": "What would you cut first if income fell by a fifth?"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "failure",
   "text": "Counting a loan as income hides the real gap."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "essentials",
   "text": "Track it, label it, review it weekly."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "check",
   "text": "Can you say where the last 500 shillings went?"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "The table"
  },
